            <ArticleTitle>[Prognostic significance of the clinical symptoms of cervical cancer].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>38-42</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The prognostic value of the basic clinical manifestations of cervical carcinoma is assessed. It is found that the rate of growth of a neoplasm may be evaluated on the basis of a relationship between the duration of previous symptoms and tumor size. Saprogenic vaginal discharge is regarded as an extremely unfavorable prognostic factor. The possible mechanism of this symptom is discussed. A quantitative procedure for evaluation of cervical carcinoma manifestations is suggested. This method was shown to offer a means of objective assessment of the rates of radiation-induced regression of tumor. Clinical manifestations should be taken into consideration in predicting the results of radiation treatment of cervical carcinoma patients.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
